{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of the lotteries and considers differences between them negligible. This allows for a comparison based on the probability of a favorable outcome. In Lottery A, the outcome is 5 Euros with 100% probability; in Lottery B, it is 5000 Euros with 0.1% probability and 0 otherwise. If the difference between 5 Euros and 5000 Euros is considered negligible (as per the reason), then the relevant factor becomes which lottery offers a higher chance of a positive payoff. Lottery A has a 100% chance of a positive outcome, while Lottery B has only a 0.1% chance. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A because it has a higher probability of a favorable (i.e., non-zero) outcome.",
